# Testing disabled

Until the user turns this back on:

- Do not run `flutter test`, `flutter analyze` for test files, or any other test command after changes.
- Do not add, update, or generate unit tests, widget tests, or fake test helpers.
- Do not read or apply the attendance-unit-tests skill unless the user asks for tests.
- Ship feature and bug-fix work without a test pass in the same change.

Only run or write tests when the user explicitly asks (for example "run tests" or "add unit tests").
